    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Rural wharves constructed or rehabilitated 
Indicator: At least 12 wharves, jetties and ramps constructed or rehabilitated by 2015 
Progress/Status: Achieved: five wharves rehabilitated, and two landing ramps constructed by 2013. Siota in Central Province, Nu&amp;apos;usi in Malaita Province, Mbunikalo in Western Province, Katurasele in Choiseul Province and Manikaraku in Guadalcanal Province. Landing ramps were constructed in Siota and Mbunikalo.
Seven wharves and one landing ramp completed 2014-16: Ringgi in Western Province, Keru in Western Province, Ngasini in Western Province, Tatamba in Isabel Province, Susubona in Isabel Province, Lambulambu in Western Province, Vuranggo in Choiseul Province, Lengana in Western Province, and a landing ramp at Uhu in Malaita Province. Vuranggo wharf has operational limitations due to its proximity to shallow water which prevents access to larger ships- it is unclear whether this was a pre-existing shallow, or caused by sand movements following the wharf construction.
 
Data Source: Project progress reports

